sts, tidus and andronicus and all j.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90s Part 7: The Other Genres","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=amHre9ZZFkU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Subject Matter Connection to Geek Rock","body":"The Decemberists are included in the discussion of geek rock due to the specific subject matter of some of their songs, implying a thematic alignment with the genre's characteristics. \"Given the subject matter of some of the Decemberist songs, you might want to include them.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of Nerd Rock","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h6snk0m4200"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"Shortlist Music Prize (2005) — Picaresque","body":"Nominated.","year":2005,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7502207"}]}],"concerts":[],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Appeal to Tweetpop Fans","body":"Death Cab for Cutie is mentioned as a band that appeals to Tweetpop fans, implying their music aligns with the genre's introspective, melodic, and emotionally sensitive qualities. This makes them a fitting choice for listeners who identify as shy, introspective, and find much contemporary music too loud or aggressive. \"And the decemberists tend to appeal to most Tweet fans, same thing with Death Cab for Cutie.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Death Cab for Cutie","from_id":151580729960193,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Twee Pop: A History","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jhgZrwtYE2g"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Contemporary Geek Rock Bearer","body":"Public Service Broadcasting was identified as one of today's flag-flyers for Geek Rock, continuing the tradition of bands that incorporate intellectual and technological themes into their music. \"Today's flyers of the flag include public service broadcasting, the decemberists, tidus and andronicus and all j.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Public Service Broadcasting","from_id":201011841966686,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90s Part 7: The Other Genres","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=amHre9ZZFkU"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Contemporary Geek Rock Bearer","body":"Titus Andronicus was identified as one of today's flag-flyers for Geek Rock, demonstrating how the genre's themes of social awkwardness and intellectual interests continue to resonate in modern alternative music. \"Today's flyers of the flag include public service broadcasting, the decemberists, tidus and andronicus and all j.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Titus Andronicus","from_id":190825498389617,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90s Part 7: The Other Genres","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=amHre9ZZFkU"}]}],"charts":[{"id":69750017263912,"type":"album","name":"Castaways and Cutouts","list_id":216253704998822,"list":"RYM Top — Folk — Indie Folk","src":"musthear","rank":96,"year":2002,"note":null,"yt":"q7FVgfGtzsA","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":69750017263912,"type":"album","name":"Castaways and Cutouts","list_id":44844465110460,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Folk Rock","src":"musthear","rank":191,"year":2002,"note":null,"yt":"q7FVgfGtzsA","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":69750017263912,"type":"album","name":"Castaways and Cutouts","list_id":76687108203,"list":"Scaruffi 2000s","src":"musthear","rank":322,"year":2002,"note":null,"yt":"q7FVgfGtzsA","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":119712958120802,"type":"album","name":"The Tain","list_id":76687108203,"list":"Scaruffi 2000s","src":"musthear","rank":735,"year":2004,"note":null,"yt":"i44Gc6N80mc","scaruffi":7.5},{"id":50735365124165,"type":"album","name":"Picaresque","work_year":2005,"list_id":44735175437010,"list":"AOTY Must Hear 2000s","src":"charts","rank":265,"year":2005,"note":null,"yt":"3uhL1npXgTI","sc